\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
Backing up Windows systems requires handling locked runtime database states and modern power-saving behavior.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\sb140\sa120\keepn\f3\fs28\b\dbch\af9\ql\sb140\sa120\ltrpar{\loch
Windows Wake-On-LAN (WoL)}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
Because Windows clients frequently sleep or hibernate when idle, the configuration must explicitly declare the target physical MAC address }{\loch
and net segment }{\loch
inside }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af8\loch
busyback.conf}{\loch
 to guarantee the device is powered up prior to rsync initialization.}
