VSS-Backed Rsync Engine}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
Windows locks system files and active user profiles (e.g., Outlook }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af8\loch
.pst}{\loch
 files, database files) during normal operation. Standard rsync binaries will fail to read these files. To bypass this, the Windows target must execute an rsync client that is fully integrated with the native }{\loch\b\loch
Volume Shadow Copy Service (VSS)}{\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af5 \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\f5\dbch\af5 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls6 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
Client Path:}{\loch
 The target binary path used on Windows systems is: }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af8\loch
'c:/Program Files/True_Blade_Systems/tb-rsync-vss-64.exe'}
\par \pard\plain \s19\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af5 \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\f5\dbch\af5 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls6 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch\b\loch
Rsync Options:}{\loch
 The configuration must include flags matching the technical capabilities of the VSS engine, prioritizing path translation formatting compatible with shadow volumes (e.g., }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af8\loch
/cygdrive/c/}{\loch
 syntax mappings).}
